<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner unit wins Mexico's Pemex deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner unit wins Mexico's Pemex deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Kvaerner ASA said on Friday its 40-percent owned Mexican subsidiary, Mecanica de la Pena, had won three contracts from state oil firm Pemex worth a total of 330 million crowns.</p>
<p>Kvaerner said the contracts were for the renovation and expansion of two refineries for Pemex. The work would include building a plant for recycling sulphur and for the treatment of gas.</p>
<p>Kvaerner John Brown would be involved in the design, planning and following up of the project, the company said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
